      "en": "**managed kubernetes** (DigitalOcean, GKE Autopilot, EKS, AKS) runs the control plane and upgrades; you manage the workloads. A **node pool** = a group of same-size servers (a small pool for main and webhooks, an autoscaling pool for workers). Keep databases and Redis managed outside the cluster — simpler and safer than StatefulSets."
